@startuml
' Figure - Use Case Diagram: authentication and administration
!include _header.txt
left to right direction

actor "Read-Only Auditor" as RO
actor "Administrator"     as ADM
ADM --|> RO

rectangle "Authentication and Administration" {
  usecase "Sign in"                as UC40
  usecase "Sign out"               as UC41
  usecase "Present second factor"  as UC42
  usecase "Enrol second factor"    as UC43
  usecase "Withdraw second factor" as UC44
  usecase "List accounts"          as UC45
  usecase "Create account"         as UC46
  usecase "Change account function" as UC47
  usecase "Suspend or restore account" as UC48
  usecase "Release a locked account"   as UC49
  usecase "Configure risk weights"     as UC50
  usecase "Issue signing credentials"  as UC51
  usecase "Record the attempt"         as UC52
}

RO  --> UC40
RO  --> UC41
RO  --> UC43
RO  --> UC44
ADM --> UC45
ADM --> UC46
ADM --> UC47
ADM --> UC48
ADM --> UC49
ADM --> UC50

UC40 ..> UC52 : <<include>>
UC46 ..> UC51 : <<include>>
UC42 .> UC40  : <<extend>>

note right of UC42
  Presenting a second factor EXTENDS
  signing in: it occurs only when the
  account has one enrolled.
end note

note bottom of UC40
  Signing in is NOT included by the other
  use cases. Authentication is a precondition
  of the subject as a whole, not a step
  repeated inside each use case.
end note
@enduml
